deny_file by the real path too: CVE-2015-1419, the part of its fix that vsftpd-ext
lacks. Ours (azsupport/ports, 12.11.2026) on vsftpd-ext 3.0.3.1 and our
patch-deny_file, from Debian (sid 3.0.5-1: 0050-CVE-2015-1419.patch of SUSE,
0070-realpath_wrapper.patch and the fix of its typo in
0082-debian-bugfixes-tls-utf8.patch; https://bugs.debian.org/776922).
vsftpd-ext has the rest of the fix of SUSE already (the filter on the last component
of the path, the whole path for a pattern that starts with "/"), and the greedy "*" of
Debian's 0006-greedy.patch (Red Hat bz 392181): with deny_file={*.php} an upload
named a.php.x.php is refused. What it lacks is realpath(): the checks see the path as
the client wrote it, so a symbolic link made in the tree of the FTP user other than by
FTP (by a site, say) led past them: with deny_file={*.mp3,.private}, pub/link/secret
where pub/link points to .private was read and an upload to pub/link/new.txt went into
.private, and pub/s.txt pointing to a.mp3 was read.
access.c: vsf_access_check_file() checks the real path too (realpath(3); for a name
that does not exist yet, as that of an upload or a new directory, the real path of its
directory and the name: vsf_sysutil_realpath() of sysutil.c, the wrapper of Debian's
0070), with the same checks as the path as written: the filter, the whole of
deny_file in it, each directory on its way (patch-deny_file). Unlike Debian's 0050,
the filter itself is unchanged: hide_file and the listings do not resolve each name
(a name of a listing is relative to the listed directory, not to the current one).
Safe: it only denies more, never less; a path that cannot be resolved is checked as
written only, as before.
Tested on Linux and by tools/servers-test.sh, with deny_file={*.mp3,*.mov,.private,*.php}:
the SIZE of pub/link/secret and /pub/link/secret (pub/link -> .private) and of pub/s.txt
(-> a.mp3) refused (without the patch: read), the upload of pub/link/new.txt refused
(stored in .private), that of pub/up/a.php.x.php refused (with and without), of
pub/up/a.txt stored. vsftpd-ext and vsftpd-ext-openssl carry the same file.

--- access.c
